For $j\ge 2$: $m=jk-1\ge 2k-1>k$. Every number greater than $k$ and at most $2023$ is **already placed** in the chain, while $m=2024$ (if it occurs) is also already placed. Hence every alternative with $j\ge 2$ is either $>2024$ (invalid) or already used. The only available choice is $m=k-1$.

